# Statement ↔ manual reconciliation

Home has **no import form**. Statements are uploaded on **Reconcile** (`/spending/reconcile`). Home shows a Statements month list (5 by default, View all expands). Every month row opens Reconcile.

Home statuses (`_home_statement_months`): `imported` (session confirmed) · `in_progress` (uploads or auto-match) · `imported_without_recon` (ledger bank txs, no session) · `not_started`. Empty staging sessions stay `not_started`.

## Manual fuzzy match (`_daily_budget_fuzzy_match_manual`)

Used on preview (`_apply_spending_preview_duplicate_marks`) and import (`spending_statement_import`).

- Same `direction`; skip `bank_matched` and `exclude_ids`
- **Date** statement on or up to `DAILY_BUDGET_MANUAL_MATCH_DATE_SLACK_DAYS` (3) after manual — not before
- **Amount** must match **exactly** (2dp); slight differences are not auto-matched
- If **one** candidate matches date+amount → accept even when payment refs / titles differ
- If several collide → require description ratio ≥ `DAILY_BUDGET_MANUAL_MATCH_RATIO` (0.72) to disambiguate
- Claim via `_daily_budget_claim_manual_match` (may store `manual_amount` / `manual_date` when bank differs)
- **Preview suggestions:** missed rows get up to `DAILY_BUDGET_MANUAL_SUGGEST_LIMIT` near-miss manuals (`preview_manual_suggestions`) with looser date/amount windows (`DAILY_BUDGET_MANUAL_SUGGEST_AMOUNT_TOL`) — native select in the Match column; choosing one marks **Skip — matched** and unchecks the row. On **Import**, those picks are sent as `manual_reconcile_claims` and persisted with `bank_matched` (so they drop from later statement previews / the unclaimed sidebar). Netted picks claim every part id; part amounts are preserved.
- **Netted suggestions:** when 2–`DAILY_BUDGET_MANUAL_SUGGEST_NET_MAX_PARTS` manuals in the date window sum **exactly** to the statement amount, offer a `kind: netted` option (preferred over singles)

## Preview flags

| Field | Values | UI |
|---|---|---|
| `preview_duplicate` + `preview_duplicate_reason` | `ledger` / `upload` / `manual` | Amber/blue/green pills; unchecked by default |
| `preview_review_reason` | `missed` / `expected_bill` | Red “Not in manual” / gray “Expected bill”; still included |

- **missed** — outgoing statement row not matching ledger fingerprint, upload dupe, manual, or included `daily_budget.plan.bill_items`
- **expected_bill** — `_match_expected_bill_item` (label sim ≥ `SPENDING_EXPECTED_BILL_SIM_THRESHOLD`, amount close); one bill claimed per row
- Summary: `preview_missed_manual`, `preview_expected_bill`
- Client `recomputeSpendingPreviewDuplicates` preserves server `manual` / review marks when direction unchanged (`data-server-*`)
- **Unclaimed manuals sidebar:** `summary.unmatched_manuals` lists manuals in the report month that are not `bank_matched` and not auto-claimed in this preview; on wide desktops the panel is portaled to `document.body` and `position: fixed` in the right viewport gutter (vertical position tracks the preview table via `syncUnclaimedManualsGutterPosition`) so it is not trapped by `.card` `backdrop-filter`; narrower viewports stack it under the table


