# Month reconcile session (`/spending/reconcile`)

Dedicated triage page: stage **multiple** statement uploads for one month, auto-match against manuals, review queue, confirm once.

## Storage

`spending.reconcile_sessions["YYYY-MM"]` — `{ report_month, status, auto_match_ran, uploads[], excluded_manual_ids[], kept_manual_ids[], reviewed_unclaimed }`.

Each upload: `{ id, file_name, bank_source, period_start, period_end, rows[] }`. Row: `{ id, date, description, amount, direction, category, include, manual_match, transfer_pair, ledger_duplicate, reconcile_mark }`.

## Match kinds (`manual_match`)

- `single` — 1 bank row → 1 manual
- `netted_manuals` — 1 bank row → N manuals (exact sum)
- `netted_banks` — N bank rows → 1 manual (shared `group_key` on every leg)

## API routes

- `GET /spending/reconcile` — page
- `GET /api/spending/reconcile/<month>` — session payload (rows, manuals, totals, queue)
- `POST .../upload` — extract file → append upload. Form: `file`, optional `bank_source`, optional `period_start` / `period_end` (defaults to full month).
- `DELETE .../upload/<id>`
- `POST .../auto-match` — fuzzy + forward/reverse net + transfer pairs
- `POST .../link-manual`, `.../unlink-manual`, `.../link-transfer`, `.../unlink-transfer`, `.../relink-netted`
- `PATCH .../row/<id>` — `{ include, direction, reconcile_mark }` (`bill` or null)
- `POST .../exclude-manual`, `.../keep-manual`, `.../review-unclaimed`
- `POST .../confirm` — requires `auto_match_ran`; if unclaimed manuals remain, requires `reviewed_unclaimed`

- Duplicate detection (`_reconcile_apply_duplicate_marks`) ignores fingerprints on **manual** txs. Claimed manuals copy the bank fingerprint; counting those as already-imported would zero `statement_count` after Find matches / a rematch.

## UI (`@templates/reconcile.html`, `@static/reconcile.js`, `@static/style.css`)

Linear 3-step wizard (one screen at a time): **Add files** → **Review** → **Import**.

- `.reconcile-page .hidden { display: none !important }` — required because steps/triage/footers use `display: flex`/`grid`/`inline-flex`, which otherwise beat Tailwind `.hidden`.
- Composer only on step 1. Custom file control (`#reconcile-file-name`). Collapsed **Adjust date range** (`#reconcile-range-toggle`). One primary CTA: **Find matches**.
- After auto-match, skip exact matches and unmatched rows with **no exact-amount suggestion** (fuzzy ±£5 near-misses wait until import as unaccounted + leftover manuals). Review queue is transfers, netted bank groups, and unmatched rows with an **exact** amount suggestion. Exact unmatched are shown first. Recap is the current task only plus a quiet matched count — progress **N of M** lives in the nav.
- **N of M** uses stable `item_key`s (`transfer:<pair_key>`, `netted:<group_key>`, `unmatched:<row_id>`). Decided keys stay decided even when “not a match” unlinks a netted group and new legs appear — those new items **append**, so the counter goes to 2 of 19 rather than resetting to 1. Undo replaces Prev when an undo is available (`POST .../relink-netted` restores a netted group).
- Actions are **Looks right** / **Not a match** on transfers, netted groups, and exact unmatched. **This is a bill** is only on **individual unmatched bank rows** (review card or Import → unaccounted) — never on net groups. Bills are not logged as manuals; they live on Daily → Plan. PATCH `/row/<id>` accepts `reconcile_mark: "bill"` (or null to unmark). Confirm imports bill-marked rows with a Daily bill category via `_reconcile_bill_import_category`.
- Leftover spending (per-row Keep/Ignore plus **Keep all** / **Ignore all**; `POST .../keep-manual` and `.../exclude-manual` accept `manual_ids[]`), a **matched spending** sample (5 rows, `<details>` to show all; each row is a Bank vs Spending comparison, amber amount/date when they differ), bill comparison, and unaccounted bank rows are on the **Import** page. Unaccounted rows can be ignored or marked as a bill. Confirm auto-POSTs `reviewed_unclaimed`. Payload includes `expected_bills` / `expected_bills_total` from Daily → Plan `bill_items`. Totals: `bill_marked_*`, `unaccounted_bank_*`.
- Do not use a status chip as navigation.
- `status == imported` is read-only (`session.readonly`, `body.reconcile-readonly`) — composer and import CTA hidden; summary lists files, outgoing, incoming (non-transfer), transfers, matches, bills, new outgoing, leftover kept, and ignored. Totals include `incoming_count` / `incoming_total` / `ignored_bank_count`.
- Match rows are a comparison grid (role · name · amount · date · source). Actions live in `.reconcile-triage-foot`.
- **Mobile (≤768px):** primary review action is full width, secondary actions share the next row; leftover/unaccounted Keep/Ignore sit under the copy (not a side column); month picker stretches; reconcile buttons are 44px tall. Nav is a 3×2 grid (Home/Daily/Monthly · Search/Reconcile/Loans); ≥768px is a single nowrap row.
- `#reconcile-view-all-toggle` expands a row table under Review.
- `bank_matched_via`: `reconcile_auto` | `reconcile_user`. Excluded manuals get `reconcile_excluded_month` on confirm.

